member.summary:
Entry point of the store engine for credential handling. Implementations talk to App Store Connect and Google Play;
tests use a fake. The secret is the JSON the user pasted: for Apple {"issuerId","keyId","privateKey"}, for
Google the service account key file as downloaded.

What a handler sees of its job and how it reports progress. Every step call renews the job's lease, publishes a live
event and, at most about once a second, checks whether a member cancelled the job (then it throws
).

The per app compliance timeline (docs/urun-plani.md 12.4): every catalog rule with a date (or a target API or SDK
minimum) that applies, or may apply, to the app, with its state. Assisted rules are done when their step is recorded;
target API and SDK rules are decided from the app profile; the rest is unknown until storeasy can check it.

A change plan before it is saved: what the planner computed from the store's current content and the desired values.
 names the content keys whose current values are fingerprinted ();
 names what is read again when the plan is approved.

Inserts or updates the saved answer document of  of an app. A non empty
 is sealed (envelope encryption bound to the app) and replaces the sealed one;
 removes it; otherwise the sealed password stays. Returns the row id.
